verdicts.reason:
Verdict upheld: no extra install.

Requirement and owner. The job is already owned as token-efficiency/statusline (current_owners index 29, class FINAL: claude-hud 0.10.0 plus the Codex footer). It lies inside two-client coding work and observability (rule A1), and the packet names the HUD under the user's 2026-10-04 directive (A3). Decider A ended deadline_exceeded with 0 chars, so the verdict rests on decider B and critic C alone.

claude-hud passes every gate live:
- unarchived; last main commit 2026-10-01; v0.10.0 is still the latest release;
- CI, Build dist and the tag-triggered Release workflow (npm test plus coverage) all succeeded at tag commit 75683c6;
- SECURITY.md exists; install is documented with Linux and WSL notes;
- local-only, no network requests; the plugin adds only two commands and no hooks.

Owner string. It holds with one precision. Claude Code natively renders subagent rows in its agent panel (statusline.md L1118-1131), while claude-hud's agents and todos lines are off by default (README L276). Codex documents /agent and footer items that include task-progress and the 5-hour and weekly limits.

ccstatusline is not clearly stronger. Its real advantages are npm SLSA provenance and two active committers. Against that, it has:
- no security policy at any of three paths;
- 161 open issues and PRs against claude-hud's 2;
- a release 14 days older;
- no worker-state widgets and no Codex support;
- a benchmark that measures Windows invocation overhead, not rendering.

Named frameworks and other candidates:
- OMC has a strong checklist, but its HUD resolves from the OMC plugin (README L331-332, L477). Adopting it would import hooks, agents and skills that overlap the native owners kept by the sibling sub-slots, and the fewer-moving-parts rule decides.
- OMX's HUD is a tmux surface for OMX's own teams.
- OmO and oh-my-pi are standalone runtimes with no Claude Code or Codex status integration.
- ohmyzsh fails the release/tag gate (0 tags, 0 releases); its codex plugin is shell completion only.
- Agent Teams AI and AO are controllers that spawn their own workers, which is a different job.

The packet's two upstream citations (claude-code CHANGELOG v2.1.289 L528, the Ultracode toggle; codex lib.rs L1327, multi_agent) are orchestration evidence, not status-display evidence.

Overturn check. The verdict's Harbor latency check is acceptable. A checklist-level trigger fits this round better: a candidate adds a security policy and worker-state rendering while claude-hud loses tag-CI or maintenance standing.
